      "math_academy_id": "e-8914",
      "problem": "Given that $P(K|L) = 0.15,$ $P(K) = 0. 6,$ and $P(L) = 0.4,$ compute $P(L|K).$",
      "worked_solution": "Using Bayes' theorem, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(L|K) & =\\frac{P(K|L)P(L)}{P(K)} \\\\  & =\\frac{(0.15)(0.4)}{0.6} \\\\  & =\\frac{0.06}{0.6} \\\\  & =0.1.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
